# Supabase autonomous migrations

When adding or changing database columns/tables:

- Run the SQL yourself. Do not ask the user to paste SQL in the Supabase dashboard.
- Read `SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN` and `SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF` from `.env.local` (gitignored).
- Execute with `node scripts/run-supabase-sql.mjs --file <sql-file>` or inline SQL.
- Also keep the matching statements in `supabase/*.sql` so the repo stays the source of truth.
- Never commit `.env.local`, access tokens, or service keys.
- Never prefix management tokens with `VITE_`.
